---
import Layout from "@layouts/ComponentsLayout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Skip link</h1>
  <p class="govuk-body-l">
    Use the skip link component to help keyboard-only users skip to the main
    content on a page
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Example</h2>
  <a
    href="#test-target-element"
    class="govuk-skip-link"
    data-module="govuk-skip-link">Skip to main content</a
  >

  <!-- GOVUK_GUIDANCE:START (auto-generated - edited content will be overwritten by scripts/update-component-guidance.mjs) -->
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">When to use this component</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    All GOV.UK pages must include a skip link. Usually, you should place the
    skip link immediately after the opening <code
      ><body></body> tag. However, if you're using a <a
        class="govuk-link"
        href="https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/cookie-banner/"
        >Cookie banner component</a
      >, place the skip link immediately after the cookie banner.</code
    >
    <p class="govuk-body">
      Some automated accessibility testing tools may warn that the skip link
      element is not inside a landmark. This warning does not apply to skip
      links, so you can ignore it. Do not wrap the skip link in a <code
        ><nav></nav> region, or move it inside the header.</code
      >
      <!-- GOVUK_GUIDANCE:END -->
    </p>
  </p>
</Layout>
